==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Brainwashed UFO Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Brainwashed Flying Cat''' after obtaining from [[Apocalypse (Merciless)]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Brainwashed UFO Cat, much like the original, has huge damage in compensation for minuscule health, range, and high cost. It can take care of peons with extreme ease, as the mini wave is pretty much made for this, but it also excels against the likes of [[Celeboodle]], [[Dagshund]], [[Duche]], [[Kory]], [[Dober P.D]], and even [[Bore Jr.]] He works especially well against [[Crazed Cow Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Cow Cat]] and [[Manic Lion Cat (Enemy)|Manic Lion Cat]] due to their melee nature, and can be very useful for dealing with hordes of them. Brainwashed UFO can also be used to rush into Traitless enemies' blindspots and quickly slaughter such in the case of [[Henry]], [[Dolphina]], [[Mr. Mole]], and [[Codename "Red Riding"]]. Nearly every Traitless boss enemy outranges Brainwashed UFO Cat, though. Brainwashed UFO also makes a decent substitute for [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed UFO]] against other traits if the player has yet to unlock him, with the Crazed form having no ability, but better stats, especially in Manic Form.

==='''True Form'''===
After getting his True Form, Brainwashed Flying Cat gets a guaranteed chance to [[Slow]] Traitless enemies. His range, while still inferior to lots of traitless enemies, allows him to counter the enemies he outranges even better, especially since it has a 100% uptime. Combined with his Mini-Wave, his Slow further improves his matchups against Traitless melee enemies, and allows him incredible value even if he hits a weak peon. Brainwashed Flying Cat may not get better range, but he improves considerably within his niche.

